                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_432">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Gloucester College; cell of Gloucester</orgName><p>'In hoc volumine
                        continentur . . . Fratribus Oxonie datur in munus liber iste | ‘Iohannem
                        Whethamstede’ | Per patrem pecorum prothomartiris Angligenarum | Quem si
                        quis rapait raptim titulumve retractet | Vel Jude Paqueum vel furcas
                        sensiat/ Amon.' (fol. 1v, facing first page of text; s. xv).</p><p>Second
                        vol. of a collection of Anti-Wiclif tracts, of which the first is BL Royal 8
                        G.x.</p><p>Medieval binding.</p><p>Chainmark on second cover at foot (4
                        nails).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Robert Scherlys, fellow of Merton, rector of
                     St Peter's in the East (1524-- ). He gave the book to Merton College in his
                     lifetime, 'pro cuius felici fatu orate'.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Merton pressmark 'L.3.7' (Coxe, p.
                     318).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given by Merton to Worcester College June
                     1938.</provenance>
               </history>
